by hand under the proposed rules. Claude has sent Codex the first question: does it read Codex's review the same way? Waiting on Codex."},"origin":"captured","project":"main"},"inbox-item:2026-11-04.ids-need-strict-order":{"entity_type":"inbox-item","entity_id":"2026-11-04.ids-need-strict-order","derived_state":"closed","event_type_sequence":["entity.created","entity.extended","entity.extended","entity.accepted","entity.completed"],"attributes":{"summary":"The first test found a flaw. Records written in the same second came out in a random order. A fix was patched into the folder's rules. The real tool still needs ids that always go up, and the agreement needs an ordering rule for two writers."},"origin":"captured","project":"main"},"inbox-item:2026-11-04.contract-v1-draft":{"entity_type":"inbox-item","entity_id":"2026-11-04.contract-v1-draft","derived_state":"closed","event_type_sequence":["entity.created","entity.extended","entity.extended","entity.extended","entity.accepted","entity.superseded"],"attributes":{"summary":"Claude and Codex need one written agreement on how the shared mailbox works before either builds anything. Claude has drafted it from the plan, Codex's review and the hand test. Codex hasn't reviewed it yet, and Al hasn't accepted it. Four questions are still open."},"origin":"captured","project":"main"},"inbox-item:2026-11-04.contract-v2-review":{"entity_type":"inbox-item","entity_id":"2026-11-04.contract-v2-review","derived_state":"closed","event_type_sequence":["entity.created","entity.extended","entity.accepted","entity.completed"],"attributes":{"summary":"The simpler agreement needs Codex to look at it and Al to accept it. Codex has been told. Nothing on Codex's side is built against the old version, so nothing breaks."},"origin":"captured","project":"main"}},"relationships":[{"from":"plan:T1-agent-messaging","to":"plan:T2-messaging-v1","type":"spawns","source":"event","source_event_id":"04b4e82f-92bd-4f06-8993-e99c8bbc6343"},{"from":"plan:T1-agent-messaging","to":"plan:M1-first-roundtrip","type":"spawns","source":"event","source_event_id":"a95fc6c3-6274-4e98-a18f-cc18f24a5e4f"},{"from":"plan:T2-messaging-v1","to":"plan:T3-claude-mail-tool","type":"spawns","source":"event","source_event_id":"f2f36a97-fcee-4e44-8ead-248c751bc883"},{"from":"plan:T2-messaging-v1","to":"plan:T3-claude-router","type":"spawns","source":"event","source_event_id":"0d07046d-dff1-4f7a-b59f-f577c73294d9"},{"from":"plan:T2-messaging-v1","to":"plan:T3-claude-session-skills","type":"spawns","source":"event","source_event_id":"ddcc31dd-bc12-48d0-b68f-1a330f1fdb11"},{"from":"plan:T2-messaging-v1","to":"plan:T3-codex-capability-trial","type":"spawns","source":"event","source_event_id":"11196636-9ae1-46f8-b7f4-a6a6a2ad40ed"},{"from":"plan:T2-messaging-v1","to":"plan:T3-codex-relay","type":"spawns","source":"event","source_event_id":"6d0b2af9-0858-46f3-9437-94875f5f1ded"},{"from":"plan:T2-messaging-v1","to":"plan:T3-codex-session-skills","type":"spawns","source":"event","source_event_id":"d3054307-e885-4215-a427-57d4084d40e0"},{"from":"plan:M1-first-roundtrip","to":"plan:T3-claude-mail-tool","type":"spawns","source":"frontmatter","source_event_id":null},{"from":"plan:M1-first-roundtrip","to":"plan:T3-claude-router","type":"spawns","source":"frontmatter","source_event_id":null},{"from":"plan:M1-first-roundtrip","to":"plan:T3-claude-session-skills","type":"spawns","source":"frontmatter","source_event_id":null},{"from":"plan:M1-first-roundtrip","to":"plan:T3-codex-capability-trial","type":"spawns","source":"frontmatter","source_event_id":null},{"from":"plan:M1-first-roundtrip","to":"plan:T3-codex-relay","type":"spawns","source":"frontmatter","source_event_id":null},{"from":"plan:M1-first-roundtrip","to":"plan:T3-codex-session-skills","type":"spawns","source":"frontmatter","source_event_id":null}],"decisions":[{"event_id":"6cc32ae7-4368-46ef-bd78-d08f490434fb","text":"Al wanted Claude and Codex on a real mailbox quickly, without building things nobody needs yet. So only the hand-run first slice is approved. The automatic relay, the router and the session skills stay as drafts until real use shows they're needed.","explains_arcs":["d675ee01-2c3a-4ce0-a422-a850e4785b04","271a44fa-9cf3-4d52-9e1f-95def1a30d4a","1fb6b3f6-325f-44d3-9ebd-5b4000bbb3cf","5223e4c3-40cf-4c3e-8557-680ccfc229bb"]},{"event_id":"389a7d8a-22ba-4aff-9be2-7d77735dc531","text":"Both ends are AI agents who can work out what's needed and ask each other. Code that decided for them only added parts to break. So the mailbox just stores, routers just nudge, and agents do the judging. File safety stays in code, because agents can't reason their way around a corrupted file.","explains_arcs":["2d027d2d-20c6-4777-8669-b7e78cc9e196"]},{"event_id":"8c012e1a-fccb-42d2-88a9-80c11e9f8be8","text":"The first agreement was written as if the two ends were programs that needed rules for everything. They're agents that can reason and ask each other, so the simpler version replaces it.","explains_arcs":["028b8249-22f9-43c1-812d-e0c64e9b4b38"]}],"summary_stats":{"total_events":115,"draft_count":0,"live_count":6,"dormant_count":0,"closed_count":7,"orphaned_count":0,"unknown_count":0},"milestone_progress":{"M1-first-roundtrip":{"scheduled_t3_count":6,"completed_t3_count":3,"live_t3_count":3}},"attention":{"pending_acceptance":[],"pending_closure":[],"deferred_verifications":[]},"latest_summary_by_entity":{},"summaries":{}}